=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough inspection of every layer of the dc_clos_bgp topology — data plane, BGP control plane, and interface hardware state — reveals no fault whatsoever.

**Data plane:** Live pings from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) and in the reverse direction both complete 5/5 with 0 % packet loss. A traceroute confirms a clean four-hop path: pc_0_0 → leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_0 → leaf_router_0_1 → pc_0_1, with sub-2 ms RTT.

**BGP control plane:** All five eBGP sessions on every router are in the Established state and exchanging the expected prefix counts. leaf_router_0_0 (AS 65200) has two valid BGP paths to 10.0.1.0/24 in its RIB — one via spine_router_0_0 (AS_PATH 65100 65201, selected as best) and one via spine_router_0_1 (AS_PATH 65101 65201, alternate). Symmetrically, leaf_router_0_1 holds two paths to 10.0.0.0/24. super_spine_router_0 holds both leaf /24 prefixes via two independent next-hops (spine_router_0_0 and spine_router_0_1). Single-path forwarding on the leaves is standard BGP best-path selection (lower router-ID tiebreaker on equal-length AS paths) — not a misconfiguration — and spine_router_0_1 provides a working hot-standby path for both prefixes.

**Interfaces:** Every interface on every device (leaf_router_0_0/0_1, spine_router_0_0/0_1, super_spine_router_0) shows state UP with zero errors, zero drops, and zero collisions. PC default gateways (10.0.0.1 and 10.0.1.1) are correctly set and reachable. No ACLs, route-maps, or filters exist on any router.

**Root cause:** There is no fault. The ticket's premise is incorrect — connectivity between pc_0_0 and pc_0_1 has never been broken in this lab state.

**Corrective action:** No network change is needed. Investigate whether the user's PC was misconfigured locally (wrong gateway, VPN split-tunnel, host firewall) at the time the symptom was observed, as the lab infrastructure is entirely healthy.
=== END ===